      "id": "lem-blowup-isomorphism-off-center",
      "concern": "Proof step 2.1 says π is 'an isomorphism of the chart overlap onto D(f_if_j)'. The whole overlap need not map there: for I=(x,y), the overlap D(y/x) contains exceptional points with x=0 and y/x≠0. The assertion needs the overlap restricted over D(f_if_j). The preceding localized-chart calculation supplies the intended gluing argument immediately.",
      "severity": "gap-a-reader-closes"
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-hilbert-relative-regularity-and-base-change",
      "concern": "In the exact-sequence clause, step 3.1 proves K is base-flat and then applies steps 1.1–2.1 to K, which require finite presentation. The statement only explicitly assumes E and F finitely presented. Over an arbitrary base, finite presentation of this kernel needs justification, rather than the generally invalid assertion that kernels of maps between finitely presented modules are finitely presented. The Noetherian-stage flat-descent argument used in lem-hilbert-uniform-sections-after-flat-pullback supplies the missing justification.",
      "severity": "gap-a-reader-closes"
